# ANV-0064 -- global counters in the model's state made two nodes' steps
# non-commuting, and the partial-order reduction pruned real states
#
# Like ANV-0063, no seed: the input is a configuration class.
seed        = n/a -- exhaustive search, not a sampled run
binary      = anvil_dpor_test
config      = 3 voters, 1 proposal/node, 2 ticks/node, <= 3 in flight
              (test/dpor_test.cc, reduction_config())
invariant   = none of the protocol's. The exhaustive search is the ground truth
              and the reduced search is what deviated from it.
reproduce   = give ModelState a single `std::vector<WireMessage> wire` numbered
              from one `next_message_id`, and a single `proposals_used` counter
              shared by all nodes, instead of per-link queues with per-link
              sequence numbers and a per-node proposal budget.
expect      = before the fix: reduced search reports  42 distinct terminal states
              after  the fix: reduced search reports 382, exactly matching the
                              exhaustive search over the same class
witness     = the two searches' terminal-state fingerprint sets differ, and the
              reduced one is a strict subset -- the signature of a reduction
              that pruned something real, as opposed to ANV-0063's signature,
              where the reduced set contained something the exhaustive one
              lacked.
guard       = test/dpor_test.cc::test_reduction_is_sound, same assertion as
              ANV-0063. The two bugs are distinguished by which way the subset
              relation fails, which is why the assertion is equality and not
              containment.
related     = the same class of mistake in the *search* rather than in the
              state: a bound on messages in flight is not invariant under
              commutation, because two orders that end in the same state pass
              through different peaks. That is not fixed, because it is not a
              bug -- it is a constraint on where the comparison is valid. The
              test therefore also asserts `full.out_of_bounds == 0`, i.e. that
              the bound never binds in the class the two searches are compared
              over. Measured: on a class where it does bind, 42 terminal states
              against 407.
note        = api_visible: no. The general rule, which is the reason this row
              exists at all: an independence relation is a claim about the
              state *representation*, not about the system. Two nodes really do
              commute in Raft. They did not commute in this encoding of Raft,
              because the encoding threaded a global counter through both.
